<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Georgios Papadopoulos</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1919–1999</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Georgios Papadopoulos was a Greek army colonel who led the military coup of 21 April 1967 and headed the junta that ruled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a> until 1974. After the king's failed counter-coup of December 1967 he made himself Prime Minister, and later also regent. In 1973 he abolished the monarchy and became president, but he was overthrown in November 1973 by fellow officers, and after the restoration of democracy he was sentenced to life imprisonment.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/georgios-papadopoulos.jpg" alt="Georgios Papadopoulos" width="320" height="486" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Georgios_Papadopoulos_speaking_(2)_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
